OAC</collab><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Horwitz</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Official methods of analysis</article-title><source>AOAC official method 992.05 folic acid (pteroylglutamic acid) in infant formula</source><year>2000</year><volume>2</volume><edition>17th ed</edition><publisher-loc>Gaithersburg, MD</publisher-loc><publisher-name>AOAC International</publisher-name><comment>50.024&#x02013;50.6</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0016"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nilsson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Yazynina</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Str&#x000e5;lsj&#x000f6;</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Jastrebova</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Solid-phase extraction for HPLC analysis of dietary folates</article-title><source>Eur Food Res Technol</source><year>2004</year><volume>219</volume><fpage>199</fpage><lpage>204</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0017"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patring</surname><given-names>JDH</given-names></name><name><surname>Jastrebova</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Application of liquid chromatography &#x02013; electrospray ionisation mass spectrometry for determination of dietary folates: Effects of buffer nature and mobile phase composition on sensitivity and selectivity</article-title><source>J Chromatogr A</source><year>2007</year><volume>1143</volume><fpage>72</fpage><lpage>82</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17210159</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0018"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Freisleben</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Schieberle</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Rychlik</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Specific and sensitive quantification of folate vitamers in foods by stable isotope dilution assays using high-performance liquid chromatography&#x02013;tandem mass spectrometry</article-title><source>Anal Bioanal Chem</source><year>2003</year><volume>376</volume><fpage>149</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12698226</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0019"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Konings</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Roomans</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><name><surname>Dorant</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldbohm</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Saris</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>van den Brandt</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Folate intake of the Dutch population according to newly established liquid chromatography data for foods</article-title><source>Am J Clin Nutr</source><year>2001</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>765</fpage><lpage>76</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11273852</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0020"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><collab>SLV</collab><source>Food composition table &#x02013; energy and nutrients</source><year>2002</year><publisher-loc>Uppsala</publisher-loc><publisher-name>SLV</publisher-name></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0021"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><collab>Fineli</collab><source>Finnish food composition database</source><year>2004</year><publisher-loc>Helsinki</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Finnish Public Health Institute, Nutrition Unit</publisher-name></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0022"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>M&#x000f8;ller</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Saxholt</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Christensen</surname><given-names>AT</given-names></name><name><surname>Hartkopp</surname><given-names>HB</given-names></name><name><surname>Hess Ygil</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><source>Danish food composition databank, revision 6.0</source><year>2005</year><comment>Department of Nutrition, Danish Institute for Food and Veterinary Research</comment><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.foodcomp.dk/FoodInformatics">http://www.foodcomp.dk/:Food Informatics</ext-link></comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0023"><label>23</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patring</surname><given-names>JDM</given-names></name><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Yazynina</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Jastrebova</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of impact of different antioxidants on stability of dietary folates during food sample preparation and storage of extracts prior to analysis</article-title><source>Anal Chim Acta</source><year>2005</year><volume>553</volume><fpage>36</fpage><lpage>42</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0024"><label>24</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shrestha</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Arcot</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Paterson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Folate assay of food by traditional and tri-enzyme treatments using cryoprotected <italic>Lactobacillus casei</italic></article-title><source>Food Chem</source><year>2000</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>545</fpage><lpage>52</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0025"><label>25</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Simonne</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Simonne</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Eitenmiller</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Coker</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bitterness and composition of lettuce varieties grown in the southeastern United States</article-title><source>Horttechnology</source><year>2002</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>721</fpage><lpage>6</lpage></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>